{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00532",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 16.27,
      "duration_seconds": 15.33,
      "text": "It's the hands again, doctor. The tingling, it's the left, no, sorry, it's the right one that's worse, but the left has joined in as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.05,
      "end_seconds": 22.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Go on, tell me more about the tingling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.55,
      "end_seconds": 37.26,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "It's mostly at night. I wake up with the pins and needles in my fingers, and I have to shake them out over the side of the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.17,
      "end_seconds": 46.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Mm. And how long has it been going on this time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.75,
      "end_seconds": 66.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.83,
      "text": "Ah, let me think. Since after Christmas. About eight weeks. Or maybe nine, I lose track of the weeks since I retired."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.17,
      "end_seconds": 76.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Eight or nine weeks, and mostly at night. What about during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.78,
      "end_seconds": 97.14,
      "duration_seconds": 17.36,
      "text": "In the morning my fingers are numb, like they're not mine. It wears off once I've had my tea. And I'm after dropping a cup twice this week, which is not like me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.4,
      "end_seconds": 108.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Numb fingers in the morning, and dropped cups."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.11,
      "end_seconds": 115.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "I broke Mary's good cup. She wasn't thrilled."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.78,
      "end_seconds": 129.09,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "I'm sure she'll forgive you. Now, the last time you were here we tried a few things. How have they worked out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.31,
      "end_seconds": 140.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "The tablets help at night, I'd say. Better than before. The pregabalin, 75 mg, one at night. That's what I take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.39,
      "end_seconds": 149.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Pregabalin, 75 milligrams at night. Anything else you're taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.76,
      "end_seconds": 163.93,
      "duration_seconds": 13.17,
      "text": "The vitamin B12, the tablets, 1000 micrograms. Once a day, with breakfast. Or is it with dinner? I take it with breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.84,
      "end_seconds": 176.5,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "With breakfast is fine. And is there any pain in your neck, when you turn your head?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.43,
      "end_seconds": 182.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "No neck pain. It's clear as a bell."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.92,
      "end_seconds": 189.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "And the shoulders, any pain there, or down the arm?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.14,
      "end_seconds": 194.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "None. Just from the elbow down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.85,
      "end_seconds": 201.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "And any rash on the hands, or on the arms?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.16,
      "end_seconds": 206.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "No rash. The skin is grand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.16,
      "end_seconds": 215.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Good. Tell me, is there anything long-term in your medical history that I should remember?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.26,
      "end_seconds": 232.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.43,
      "text": "The carpal tunnel, the doctor before you called it that. And the low B12, that's why the tablets. And the arthritis in my thumb, the left one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.74,
      "end_seconds": 239.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Carpal tunnel, low B12, and thumb arthritis. Thank you. Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.98,
      "end_seconds": 247.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "None that I know of. I've never had a reaction to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.51,
      "end_seconds": 260.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "All right. Let me ask about the rest of you. How's the heart, any racing or fluttering?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.03,
      "end_seconds": 264.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "The heart is fine. Not a flutter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.27,
      "end_seconds": 269.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "And your stomach and bowels?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.69,
      "end_seconds": 276.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "All normal. I'm regular as clockwork, you could set your watch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.67,
      "end_seconds": 284.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "Good to hear. Let me take your blood pressure while we're here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.43,
      "end_seconds": 308.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Blood pressure is 126 over 78. And your pulse is 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.64,
      "end_seconds": 315.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Is that good for an old man?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.89,
      "end_seconds": 330.82,
      "duration_seconds": 12.93,
      "text": "It's very good for any man. Now, what's the thing you'd most like to be able to do with those hands again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.48,
      "end_seconds": 341.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Hold a fishing rod through the night without waking. And Mary's cups, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.01,
      "end_seconds": 358.8,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "Then those are our targets. Keep the wrist straight when you sleep, and shake the hands out in the morning before you pick up anything hot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.51,
      "end_seconds": 365.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I'll put a note on the kettle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.97,
      "end_seconds": 379.07,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "Do. Stay with the same tablets for now. I'd like to see you again in six weeks, and we'll see where things stand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.82,
      "end_seconds": 390.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Six weeks, right. Will I remember it? I'll tell Mary to write it on the fridge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.46,
      "end_seconds": 398.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "The desk will give you a card as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.16,
      "end_seconds": 405.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Grand, grand. Thanks very much, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.03,
      "end_seconds": 412.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Mind yourself, and mind the cups."
    }
  ]
}
